<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  robot.xml — EMU v3017 Clean Blob fast training model
  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  ~0.48 kg ball-foot biped, 6 actuated DoF, 2 passive mid-shin flex DoF.

  Kinematic chain per leg:
    torso → hip_roll → hip_pitch → knee → passive mid-shin flex → ball foot

  Geometry:
    thigh:  (0,0,0) → (-0.1202, 0, -0.1202)   → 45° down-and-back at q=0
    shin:   (0,0,0) → (+0.1202, 0, -0.1202)   → 45° down-and-forward at q=0
    foot:   sphere ball, r=0.018, one main contact point

  Passive spring design — v5056 physical variant:
    Each knee has a 30mm/30mm site-to-site compression-strut equivalent.
    MuJoCo's spatial tendon spring pushes sites apart when the leg is folded:
    rest pin separation 60mm, stiffness 750 N/m, effective neutral knee
    extension torque about 0.28 N.m and deep (-55deg) about 0.90 N.m.
    This is NOT a string/tension-only cable: real hardware needs a guided
    compression cartridge (or an equivalent rocker/cam). There is NO knee
    spring torque at full extension (+90deg). Hip-pitch springs are removed,
    while hip-roll centering and passive shin flex remain unchanged.
    Physical spring stiffness is preliminary: verify COM, mass, interference,
    CPU/MJX parity, thermal loads and actual hardware before building.

  Actuators:
    Six Feetech ST-3215-C018 at 12V (6x 55g) use rated 0.980665 N.m,
    peak-stall ±2.941995 N.m and no-load 0.222s/60deg (4.717 rad/s).
    The six position actuators are HARD-LIMITED to ±0.980665 N.m at
    the actual MuJoCo/MJX force output, not the 2.941995 N.m stall rating.
    Stall torque is a data-sheet peak rating, NOT an allowed PPO force.
    A passive viscous damping coefficient of 0.624 is retained as the
    previous SIMPLIFIED motor speed/load proxy; it is NOT a true servo
    velocity-dependent electrical torque limit and damps even unpowered.
    kp=10 N.m/rad, armature=0.012 kg.m², frictionloss=0.08 N.m are
    provisional pre-existing controls, not manufacturer-calibrated values.
    Hardware needs its own 12V regulator, adequate bus current margin,
    thermal limits and mechanical load validation.

  Contact contract:
    v3017 seed model deliberately makes the thin thigh/shin rods non-contacting
    so early training cannot be dominated by blunt sentinel/proxy deaths.  Feet
    remain the only contact geoms.  Non-foot geometry is still tracked through
    a soft body-low diagnostic/penalty in environment.py, and a later validation
    model should reintroduce stricter sentinel policing before hardware trust.
-->

<mujoco>
  <compiler angle="degree" />
  <option timestep="0.005" integrator="Euler" gravity="0 0 -9.81" />

  <default>
    <!--
      Base joint defaults preserve the passive-shin model. The six motor joints
      explicitly override armature/frictionloss below so robot.xml alone fully
      defines the effective physics used by MJX.
      damping=0.624 is a crude C018 stall/no-load speed proxy; unlike an
      electrical torque-speed curve it always dissipates. Shin flex joints
      override damping to 0.08 for the passive carbon-shin compliance.
    -->
    <joint damping="0.624" armature="0.006" />
    <geom friction="1.5 0.005 0.0001" />
  </default>

  <worldbody>
    <light name="light_top" pos="0 0 2" directional="true" />

    <geom name="floor" type="plane" size="5 5 0.05" rgba="0.2 0.25 0.3 1" />
    <body name="torso" pos="0 0 0.2584">
      <freejoint name="root" />
      <!-- v3017: torso mass is shifted 26 mm forward so the neutral < stance
           has COM over/just ahead of the ball feet. v3002 had the leg rods
           pulling COM behind the contact point, causing immediate backward falls. -->
      <geom name="torso_box" type="box" size="0.05 0.09 0.025" pos="0.026 0 0" mass="0.30"
            rgba="0.8 0.1 0.1 1" />
      <site name="imu" pos="0 0 0" />

      <!-- ═══ RIGHT LEG ═══ -->
      <body name="r_hip" pos="0 -0.08 0">
        <inertial mass="0.01" pos="0 0 0" diaginertia="1e-5 1e-5 1e-5" />
        <joint name="r_hip_roll" type="hinge" armature="0.012" frictionloss="0.08" axis="1 0 0"
               range="-25 25" stiffness="2.0" springref="0" />
        <body name="r_thigh" pos="0 0 0">
          <!-- No competing hip pitch spring: progressive knee strut owns vertical support. -->
          <joint name="r_hip_pitch" type="hinge" armature="0.012" frictionloss="0.08" axis="0 1 0"
                 range="-50 50" stiffness="0" springref="0" />
          <site name="r_knee_strut_thigh" pos="-0.0989868 0 -0.0989868" size="0.003" rgba="0 0.7 0.6 1" />
          <geom name="r_thigh_rod" type="capsule" size="0.008"
                fromto="0 0 0 -0.1202 0 -0.1202" mass="0.04"
                contype="0" conaffinity="0" />
          <body name="r_shin" pos="-0.1202 0 -0.1202">
            <!-- Knee support comes from a two-site compressive spatial tendon. -->
            <joint name="r_knee" type="hinge" armature="0.012" frictionloss="0.08" axis="0 1 0"
                   range="-55 95" stiffness="0" springref="90" />
            <site name="r_knee_strut_shin" pos="0.0212132 0 -0.0212132" size="0.003" rgba="0 0.7 0.6 1" />
            <!-- Carbon shin compliance is modelled at the rod midpoint so the
                 virtual flex angle has the same semantics as the magnet/Hall
                 pair on the real shin. -->
            <geom name="r_shin_upper" type="capsule" size="0.008"
                  fromto="0 0 0 0.0601 0 -0.0601" mass="0.015"
                  contype="0" conaffinity="0" />
            <body name="r_shin_lower" pos="0.0601 0 -0.0601">
              <joint name="r_shin_flex" type="hinge" axis="0 1 0" range="-10 10"
                     stiffness="4.0" damping="0.08" />
              <geom name="r_shin_lower_rod" type="capsule" size="0.008"
                    fromto="0 0 0 0.0601 0 -0.0601" mass="0.015"
                    contype="0" conaffinity="0" />
              <body name="r_foot" pos="0.0601 0 -0.0601">
                <geom name="r_foot_ball" type="sphere" size="0.018" pos="0 0 0"
                      mass="0.010" rgba="0.25 0.35 0.80 1" />
              </body>
            </body>
          </body>
        </body>
      </body>

      <!-- ═══ LEFT LEG ═══ (mirror) -->
      <body name="l_hip" pos="0 0.08 0">
        <inertial mass="0.01" pos="0 0 0" diaginertia="1e-5 1e-5 1e-5" />
        <joint name="l_hip_roll" type="hinge" armature="0.012" frictionloss="0.08" axis="1 0 0"
               range="-25 25" stiffness="2.0" springref="0" />
        <body name="l_thigh" pos="0 0 0">
          <joint name="l_hip_pitch" type="hinge" armature="0.012" frictionloss="0.08" axis="0 1 0"
                 range="-50 50" stiffness="0" springref="0" />
          <site name="l_knee_strut_thigh" pos="-0.0989868 0 -0.0989868" size="0.003" rgba="0 0.7 0.6 1" />
          <geom name="l_thigh_rod" type="capsule" size="0.008"
                fromto="0 0 0 -0.1202 0 -0.1202" mass="0.04"
                contype="0" conaffinity="0" />
          <body name="l_shin" pos="-0.1202 0 -0.1202">
            <joint name="l_knee" type="hinge" armature="0.012" frictionloss="0.08" axis="0 1 0"
                   range="-55 95" stiffness="0" springref="90" />
            <site name="l_knee_strut_shin" pos="0.0212132 0 -0.0212132" size="0.003" rgba="0 0.7 0.6 1" />
            <!-- Carbon shin compliance is modelled at the rod midpoint so the
                 virtual flex angle has the same semantics as the magnet/Hall
                 pair on the real shin. -->
            <geom name="l_shin_upper" type="capsule" size="0.008"
                  fromto="0 0 0 0.0601 0 -0.0601" mass="0.015"
                  contype="0" conaffinity="0" />
            <body name="l_shin_lower" pos="0.0601 0 -0.0601">
              <joint name="l_shin_flex" type="hinge" axis="0 1 0" range="-10 10"
                     stiffness="4.0" damping="0.08" />
              <geom name="l_shin_lower_rod" type="capsule" size="0.008"
                    fromto="0 0 0 0.0601 0 -0.0601" mass="0.015"
                    contype="0" conaffinity="0" />
              <body name="l_foot" pos="0.0601 0 -0.0601">
                <geom name="l_foot_ball" type="sphere" size="0.018" pos="0 0 0"
                      mass="0.010" rgba="0.25 0.35 0.80 1" />
              </body>
            </body>
          </body>
        </body>
      </body>
    </body>
  </worldbody>

  <!--
    v5056: ST-3215-C018 (12 V), SAME six position-actuator channels.
    Manufacturer A/0: stall 30 kgf.cm = 2.941995 N.m, rated 10 kgf.cm
    = 0.980665 N.m, no-load 0.222s/60deg = 4.717 rad/s (45RPM),
    stall 2.7 A per motor, 55g each. DO NOT supply 12V to old C001.
    HARD position-actuator forcerange enforces rated torque at ALL times;
    it does NOT independently enforce a calibrated velocity-dependent
    electrical torque-speed envelope or thermal duty limits. Measure speed,
    torque and current before treating this as validated sim2real.
    The 0.624 N.m.s/rad damping is a heuristic (stall / no-load speed)
    that *also* damps without active drive, and can supply physically
    unrealistic passive braking. Do not treat it as actuator torque;
    report it separately and replace only after hardware measurement.
  -->
  <tendon>
    <!-- Site separation 18..60mm as knee folds -55..+90deg; compression
         pushes the points apart via MuJoCo's passive tendon spring.
         Rest length 60mm; 750N/m equivalent, 42mm max compression.
         A physical spring needs a guided strut / 2:1 rocker cartridge. -->
    <spatial name="r_knee_support" stiffness="750" springlength="0.060" width="0.002"
             rgba="0 0.7 0.6 1">
      <site site="r_knee_strut_thigh" />
      <site site="r_knee_strut_shin" />
    </spatial>
    <spatial name="l_knee_support" stiffness="750" springlength="0.060" width="0.002"
             rgba="0 0.7 0.6 1">
      <site site="l_knee_strut_thigh" />
      <site site="l_knee_strut_shin" />
    </spatial>
  </tendon>
  <actuator>
    <position name="r_hip_roll"  joint="r_hip_roll"
              kp="10" ctrlrange="-25 25"  forcelimited="true" forcerange="-0.980665 0.980665" />
    <position name="r_hip_pitch" joint="r_hip_pitch"
              kp="10" ctrlrange="-50 50"  forcelimited="true" forcerange="-0.980665 0.980665" />
    <position name="r_knee"      joint="r_knee"
              kp="10" ctrlrange="-55 95"  forcelimited="true" forcerange="-0.980665 0.980665" />
    <position name="l_hip_roll"  joint="l_hip_roll"
              kp="10" ctrlrange="-25 25"  forcelimited="true" forcerange="-0.980665 0.980665" />
    <position name="l_hip_pitch" joint="l_hip_pitch"
              kp="10" ctrlrange="-50 50"  forcelimited="true" forcerange="-0.980665 0.980665" />
    <position name="l_knee"      joint="l_knee"
              kp="10" ctrlrange="-55 95"  forcelimited="true" forcerange="-0.980665 0.980665" />
  </actuator>

  <!-- Thigh and shin rods are non-contacting in the fast seed model; feet are
       the only contact geoms. Later hardware-validation models can reintroduce
       explicit sentinel geoms without changing the training contact contract. -->

  <sensor>
    <accelerometer name="accel" site="imu" />
    <gyro          name="gyro"  site="imu" />
  </sensor>
</mujoco>